WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.731 --> 00:03.534 align:center line:81%
In 2018, at the University of Utah,

00:04.167 --> 00:08.972 align:center line:79%
a special professorship was created called
the “Dr. Russell M. Nelson

00:09.206 --> 00:14.111 align:center line:79%
and Dantzel W. Nelson Presidential
Chair in Cardiothoracic Surgery.”

00:14.511 --> 00:15.779 align:center line:81%
“Cardio” meaning heart,

00:16.213 --> 00:17.915 align:center line:81%
“thoracic” meaning chest.

00:18.782 --> 00:22.819 align:center line:79%
It honored President Nelson's
important work as a heart surgeon

00:22.819 --> 00:26.990 align:center line:79%
and the support he received
from his late wife, Dantzel.

00:27.991 --> 00:32.663 align:center line:79%
This professorship was paid for by
a fund designed to last into the future.

00:33.597 --> 00:35.766 align:center line:81%
The individual selected for this type

00:35.766 --> 00:39.536 align:center line:79%
of prestigious professorship
receives recognition,

00:39.736 --> 00:42.372 align:center line:81%
salary support, and research funds.

00:43.774 --> 00:46.910 align:center line:79%
The first surgeon chosen
to hold the professorship

00:47.277 --> 00:49.813 align:center line:81%
was Dr. Craig H. Selzman,

00:50.113 --> 00:53.216 align:center line:79%
a skilled heart surgeon
who’s not a member of the Church.

00:54.785 --> 00:59.523 align:center line:79%
At the ceremony to award
this professorship to Dr. Selzman,

00:59.823 --> 01:02.559 align:center line:81%
many important guests were in attendance,

01:02.559 --> 01:07.598 align:center line:79%
including President Nelson and his wife,
Sister Wendy W. Nelson.

01:08.498 --> 01:11.768 align:center line:79%
During the meeting,
President Nelson spoke modestly

01:11.969 --> 01:14.204 align:center line:81%
of his pioneering surgical career.

01:15.372 --> 01:19.810 align:center line:79%
Then, Dr. Selzman shared what it meant
to him to be appointed

01:19.810 --> 01:21.178 align:center line:81%
to this professorship.

01:22.012 --> 01:27.284 align:center line:79%
He related that four days earlier,
after a long day in the operating room,

01:27.718 --> 01:31.822 align:center line:79%
he discovered that one of his patients
needed to go back to surgery.

01:32.623 --> 01:34.891 align:center line:81%
He was tired and disappointed,

01:35.492 --> 01:39.129 align:center line:79%
knowing he'd have to spend
another night in the hospital.

01:40.163 --> 01:45.636 align:center line:79%
This evening, Dr. Selzman had a life-
changing conversation with himself.

01:46.570 --> 01:49.606 align:center line:81%
In the moment, he thought, “On Friday,

01:50.340 --> 01:54.277 align:center line:79%
I’ll be appointed to a professorship
named after Dr. Nelson.

01:54.778 --> 01:58.815 align:center line:79%
He was always known as someone
who kept his emotions in check,

01:59.216 --> 02:03.020 align:center line:79%
treated everyone with respect,
and never lost his temper.

02:03.153 --> 02:09.026 align:center line:79%
Now that my name will be linked with his,
I need to try to be more like him.”

02:10.093 --> 02:14.097 align:center line:79%
Doctor Selzman was already
a very considerate surgeon,

02:14.731 --> 02:17.134 align:center line:81%
but he wanted to become even better.

02:18.168 --> 02:21.972 align:center line:79%
In the past, his surgical team
might have been aware of his fatigue

02:21.972 --> 02:26.610 align:center line:79%
and frustration because he may
have let it show in his manner

02:26.610 --> 02:31.114 align:center line:79%
and tone of voice, but
in the operating room that night,

02:31.648 --> 02:37.287 align:center line:79%
Dr. Selzman made a conscientious
effort to be especially supportive

02:37.287 --> 02:38.955 align:center line:81%
and understanding of his team.

02:40.090 --> 02:42.159 align:center line:81%
He felt it made a difference

02:42.626 --> 02:47.364 align:center line:79%
and resolved to continue trying
to be more like Doctor Nelson.

02:48.665 --> 02:53.203 align:center line:79%
Five years later, President Nelson
donated his professional papers

02:53.403 --> 02:54.771 align:center line:81%
to the University of Utah.

02:55.672 --> 02:59.943 align:center line:79%
Dignitaries from the university came
to formally thank President Nelson.

03:00.811 --> 03:04.681 align:center line:79%
During this event,
Dr. Selzman spoke again.

03:05.649 --> 03:09.986 align:center line:79%
Referring to President
Nelson’s initials R M N,

03:11.088 --> 03:14.224 align:center line:81%
he said, “There is an ‘RMN’

03:14.224 --> 03:18.829 align:center line:79%
ethos that now pervades the Division
of Cardiothoracic Surgery

03:18.829 --> 03:22.599 align:center line:79%
at the University
of Utah.” In frustrating situations,

03:22.599 --> 03:24.301 align:center line:81%
Dr. Selzman explained,

03:24.634 --> 03:28.638 align:center line:79%
“I do what we now teach
our trainees to do: focus,

03:29.005 --> 03:31.241 align:center line:81%
get over it, and do the best you can.

03:31.641 --> 03:34.544 align:center line:81%
This ethos lives in us every day.

03:34.911 --> 03:39.983 align:center line:79%
We give lapel pins to every member
of the division and each new trainee.

03:40.784 --> 03:44.855 align:center line:79%
At the bottom of the pin
are the letters R M N.

03:45.856 --> 03:49.826 align:center line:79%
The RMN ethos is foundational
to our training;

03:50.293 --> 03:52.362 align:center line:81%
we teach it to everyone.”

03:53.463 --> 03:58.869 align:center line:79%
Dr. Selzman had intentionally improved
his prior attitude and aspirations

03:59.302 --> 04:03.774 align:center line:79%
because his name was now linked
to that of President Nelson.

04:05.776 --> 04:11.681 align:center line:79%
This series of events involving
Dr. Selzman caused me to ask myself,

04:12.482 --> 04:20.056 align:center line:79%
“How have I changed since I linked my name
with the name of Jesus Christ?

04:20.957 --> 04:23.994 align:center line:79%
Have I adopted a Christlike
ethos as a result?

04:24.427 --> 04:28.698 align:center line:79%
Have I genuinely tried to become
better and more like Him?”

04:29.933 --> 04:31.902 align:center line:81%
In Doctor Selzman’s experience,

04:31.902 --> 04:35.238 align:center line:79%
we can see at least five parallels
to the process through

04:35.272 --> 04:39.075 align:center line:79%
which we take upon
ourselves the name of Jesus Christ.

04:40.143 --> 04:43.013 align:center line:79%
Even though that process
begins with baptism,

04:43.713 --> 04:48.285 align:center line:79%
it’s not complete until
we are more pure and holy

04:48.552 --> 04:50.353 align:center line:81%
and have become more like Him.

04:51.721 --> 04:54.925 align:center line:81%
The first parallel is identification.

04:55.826 --> 05:00.764 align:center line:79%
Dr. Selzman’s appointment to the
Nelson professorship linked his name

05:00.764 --> 05:02.232 align:center line:81%
to President Nelson's,

05:02.232 --> 05:05.836 align:center line:79%
and Dr. Selzman began
to identify with President Nelson.

05:06.736 --> 05:09.940 align:center line:79%
When we take upon ourselves
the name of Jesus Christ,

05:09.973 --> 05:12.142 align:center line:81%
we link our name with His.

05:12.576 --> 05:14.144 align:center line:81%
We identify with Him.

05:14.644 --> 05:17.380 align:center line:81%
We gladly become known as Christian.

05:17.814 --> 05:19.616 align:center line:81%
We acknowledge the Savior

05:19.950 --> 05:23.987 align:center line:79%
and unapologetically stand up
to be counted as His.

05:25.222 --> 05:26.389 align:center line:81%
Closely related to

05:26.423 --> 05:30.393 align:center line:79%
identification is another
parallel: remembrance.

05:31.394 --> 05:34.030 align:center line:81%
When Dr. Selzman goes into his office,

05:34.231 --> 05:37.534 align:center line:79%
his eyes are drawn
to the medallion he received

05:37.534 --> 05:40.804 align:center line:79%
when he was appointed
to the Nelson professorship.

05:41.605 --> 05:46.843 align:center line:79%
This medallion reminds him daily
of the RMN ethos.

05:47.844 --> 05:52.849 align:center line:79%
For us, partaking of the sacrament
each week helps us remember

05:52.849 --> 05:55.218 align:center line:81%
Jesus Christ throughout the week.

05:56.253 --> 05:58.221 align:center line:81%
As we partake of the sacrament,

05:58.388 --> 06:03.426 align:center line:79%
we do so in remembrance
of the price He paid to redeem us.

06:04.327 --> 06:10.567 align:center line:79%
We covenant anew to remember Him,
recognize His greatness,

06:11.134 --> 06:13.503 align:center line:81%
and appreciate His goodness.

06:13.937 --> 06:16.907 align:center line:79%
We acknowledge repeatedly
that it is only in

06:16.907 --> 06:21.945 align:center line:79%
and through His grace that we’re saved
from physical and spiritual death.

06:23.046 --> 06:26.316 align:center line:79%
Remembrance means that we follow
the advice given by the Book

06:26.316 --> 06:27.684 align:center line:81%
of Mormon prophet Alma.

06:29.185 --> 06:33.456 align:center line:79%
We “let all [our] doings be unto the Lord,
and whithersoever [we go,

06:33.490 --> 06:35.292 align:center line:81%
we] let it be in the Lord; ...

06:35.692 --> 06:38.728 align:center line:79%
[we] let all [our] thoughts be
directed unto the Lord; ...

06:39.129 --> 06:44.768 align:center line:79%
and [we] let the affections of [our] heart
be placed upon the Lord forever.”

06:45.869 --> 06:50.740 align:center line:79%
Even when we’re occupied with other
matters, we remain mindful of Him,

06:51.274 --> 06:56.546 align:center line:79%
just as we remember our own name,
regardless of what else we focus on.

06:57.847 --> 07:00.984 align:center line:79%
An outgrowth of remembering
what the Savior has done

07:00.984 --> 07:04.654 align:center line:81%
for us is a third parallel: emulation.

07:05.622 --> 07:12.429 align:center line:79%
Dr. Selzman began to emulate
President Nelson and the RMN ethos.

07:13.697 --> 07:19.436 align:center line:79%
I believe President Nelson’s ethos is
simply a  manifestation

07:19.436 --> 07:23.573 align:center line:79%
of his lifelong discipleship
of Jesus Christ.

07:24.641 --> 07:29.980 align:center line:79%
For us the more we identify
with and remember Jesus Christ,

07:30.313 --> 07:32.782 align:center line:81%
the more we want to be like Him.

07:33.850 --> 07:38.755 align:center line:79%
As His disciples, we change
for the better when we focus on Him,

07:39.489 --> 07:42.425 align:center line:81%
more so than when we focus on ourselves.

07:43.059 --> 07:48.365 align:center line:79%
We strive to become like Him and seek
to be blessed with His attributes.

07:49.499 --> 07:54.604 align:center line:79%
We pray fervently to be filled
with charity, the pure love of Christ.

07:55.638 --> 07:58.008 align:center line:81%
As President Nelson taught in April,

07:59.242 --> 08:01.945 align:center line:81%
“As charity becomes part of our nature,

08:02.445 --> 08:05.248 align:center line:81%
we lose the impulse to demean others.

08:06.049 --> 08:07.884 align:center line:81%
We will stop judging others.

08:08.518 --> 08:11.688 align:center line:79%
We will have charity
for those from all walks of life.

08:12.756 --> 08:16.092 align:center line:79%
Charity towards all is essential
to our progress.

08:16.760 --> 08:22.065 align:center line:79%
Charity is the foundation of a godly
character.” Alongside charity,

08:22.665 --> 08:28.972 align:center line:79%
we seek, cultivate, and expand
other spiritual gifts from the Savior,

08:29.539 --> 08:33.877 align:center line:79%
including integrity,
patience, and diligence.

08:35.578 --> 08:41.051 align:center line:79%
Emulating Jesus Christ
leads us to a fourth parallel: alignment

08:41.051 --> 08:45.088 align:center line:79%
with His purposes.
We join Him in His work.

08:46.222 --> 08:47.357 align:center line:81%
As a surgeon,

08:47.657 --> 08:53.897 align:center line:79%
Dr. Nelson was known as a teacher,
a healer, and a researcher.

08:54.998 --> 09:00.370 align:center line:79%
The lapel pin used in Dr. Selzman’s
division emphasizes these endeavors,

09:00.370 --> 09:05.241 align:center line:79%
featuring the words teach,
heal, and discover.

09:06.743 --> 09:09.879 align:center line:79%
For us, part of taking
upon ourselves the name

09:09.879 --> 09:13.216 align:center line:81%
of Jesus Christ involves willingly,

09:13.650 --> 09:19.556 align:center line:79%
intentionally, and enthusiastically
aligning our goals with His.

09:20.190 --> 09:23.893 align:center line:79%
We join Him in His work when
we love, share, and invite.

09:24.094 --> 09:25.628 align:center line:81%
We join Him in His work

09:26.029 --> 09:27.730 align:center line:81%
when we minister to others,

09:27.997 --> 09:33.670 align:center line:79%
especially the vulnerable
and those who've been wounded, shattered,

09:34.037 --> 09:37.440 align:center line:81%
or crushed by their earthly experiences.

09:38.508 --> 09:42.846 align:center line:79%
So we more fully take
upon ourselves the name

09:42.846 --> 09:50.720 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ through identification,
remembrance, emulation, and alignment.

09:51.521 --> 09:56.559 align:center line:79%
Doing these four leads to a fifth
parallel: empowerment.

09:57.193 --> 10:01.064 align:center line:79%
We access God's power
and blessings in our lives.

10:02.465 --> 10:06.336 align:center line:79%
The Nelson professorship
provides Dr. Selzman recognition

10:06.336 --> 10:11.441 align:center line:79%
and support funds that he's using
to change the culture in his division.

10:12.275 --> 10:17.213 align:center line:79%
He applies this endowment
of power to help others. In a similar way

10:18.014 --> 10:21.384 align:center line:79%
when we take upon
ourselves the name of the Savior,

10:21.985 --> 10:27.390 align:center line:79%
our Heavenly Father blesses us with His
power to help us fulfill our mission

10:27.390 --> 10:28.424 align:center line:81%
in mortality.

10:29.626 --> 10:32.195 align:center line:81%
As we make additional covenants with God,

10:32.595 --> 10:36.833 align:center line:79%
we take upon ourselves more
fully the name of Jesus Christ.

10:37.333 --> 10:43.439 align:center line:79%
Consequently, God blesses us
with more of His power. As President

10:43.473 --> 10:48.511 align:center line:79%
Nelson taught, “Each person who makes
covenants in baptismal fonts

10:48.511 --> 10:50.413 align:center line:81%
and in temples—and keeps them—

10:51.014 --> 10:55.185 align:center line:79%
has increased access
to the power of Jesus Christ. ...

10:56.119 --> 11:01.391 align:center line:79%
The reward for keeping covenants with God
is heavenly power ... [that] strengthens

11:02.025 --> 11:05.395 align:center line:79%
us to withstand our trials,
temptations, and heartaches

11:05.395 --> 11:06.396 align:center line:81%
better.”

11:07.230 --> 11:09.599 align:center line:81%
We become more spiritually receptive.

11:09.899 --> 11:14.404 align:center line:79%
We have more courage to confront
seemingly impossible circumstances.

11:15.038 --> 11:18.875 align:center line:79%
We're strengthened more
in our resolve to follow Jesus Christ.

11:19.175 --> 11:23.313 align:center line:79%
We more speedily repent and return
to Him when we transgress.

11:24.080 --> 11:28.785 align:center line:79%
We become better at sharing His gospel
with His power and authority.

11:29.619 --> 11:35.592 align:center line:79%
We help those in need while being less
judgmental, far less judgmental.

11:36.426 --> 11:38.761 align:center line:81%
We retain a remission of our sins.

11:39.562 --> 11:46.836 align:center line:79%
We have greater peace, and we're more
cheerful because we can always rejoice.

11:47.737 --> 11:52.942 align:center line:79%
His glory will be round about us,
and his angels will have charge over us.

11:54.877 --> 12:01.551 align:center line:79%
The Savior invites us,
“Come unto the Father in my name,

12:02.685 --> 12:04.854 align:center line:81%
and in due time receive of his fulness.”

12:05.855 --> 12:07.624 align:center line:81%
I urge you to do this.

12:08.458 --> 12:10.193 align:center line:81%
Come unto our Heavenly Father.

12:11.027 --> 12:16.299 align:center line:79%
Take upon yourself the name
of Jesus Christ. Identify with Him.

12:17.033 --> 12:22.639 align:center line:79%
Always remember Him. Strive
to be like Him. Join Him in His work.

12:23.273 --> 12:26.676 align:center line:79%
Receive His power
and blessings in your life.

12:27.877 --> 12:33.182 align:center line:79%
Etch His name in your heart,
willingly and intentionally.

12:34.217 --> 12:37.220 align:center line:81%
This gives you standing before God

12:37.654 --> 12:41.958 align:center line:79%
and qualifies you for the Savior's
advocacy on your behalf.

12:42.992 --> 12:47.163 align:center line:79%
You’ll become an exalted inheritor
in the kingdom of our Father in Heaven,

12:47.664 --> 12:53.102 align:center line:79%
a joint-heir with His Firstborn,
our beloved Savior and Redeemer.

12:53.903 --> 12:56.739 align:center line:81%
He lives. I absolutely know it.

12:56.906 --> 12:59.842 align:center line:81%
He loves you. He gave His life for you.

13:00.109 --> 13:03.780 align:center line:79%
He pleads with you
to come unto the Hather through Him.

13:04.113 --> 13:07.116 align:center line:81%
in the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

